# Disabled checks, and why:
#
# clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#   Flags snprintf and asks for the C11 Annex K snprintf_s instead, which glibc,
#   musl and Apple's libc do not implement. snprintf is bounded by its size
#   argument and always NUL terminates, and every call here passes sizeof of a
#   local buffer. A truncated message is the worst outcome, and these buffers
#   only ever hold exception messages.
#
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#   Monocypher's own C API and the JNI signatures fix the order of arguments
#   that share a type, so we cannot act on this.
#
# bugprone-macro-parentheses
#   Only the TO_*_CTX_CLASS, FROM_*_CTX_CLASS and FROM_ARGON2_CONFIG_CLASS
#   macros trigger it, and the off-heap context and Argon2 redesigns remove them.
#   Re-enable it once they are gone.
Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-macro-parentheses
